  <graph edgedefault="undirected">
    <node id="Inner West Local Environmental Plan 2022">
      <data key="d0">Inner West Local Environmental Plan 2022</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Inner West Local Environmental Plan 2022 outlines building height controls, floor space ratios, setback requirements, and parking requirements for various types of buildings and zones.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fddb9a116002f5fba7900393df558bd9</data>
      <data key="d4">Inner_West_LEP_2022.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1756184945</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Residential Buildings">
      <data key="d0">Residential Buildings</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Residential buildings are defined within the environmental plan as structures that must not exceed building height controls of 8.5 metres.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fddb9a116002f5fba7900393df558bd9</data>
      <data key="d4">Inner_West_LEP_2022.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1756184945</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Commercial Buildings">
      <data key="d0">Commercial Buildings</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Commercial buildings in mixed-use zones are limited to a height of 12 metres according to the plan.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fddb9a116002f5fba7900393df558bd9</data>
      <data key="d4">Inner_West_LEP_2022.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1756184945</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Mixed Use Zones">
      <data key="d0">Mixed Use Zones</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Mixed use zones refer to areas designated in the environmental plan where both commercial and residential activities can occur, with specific building and floor space ratio controls.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fddb9a116002f5fba7900393df558bd9</data>
      <data key="d4">Inner_West_LEP_2022.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1756184945</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Floor Space Ratio Controls">
      <data key="d0">Floor Space Ratio Controls</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Floor Space Ratio Controls specify the limits on the total floor area of buildings relative to the area of the block, with different limits for various zones.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fddb9a116002f5fba7900393df558bd9</data>
      <data key="d4">Inner_West_LEP_2022.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1756184945</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Parking Requirements">
      <data key="d0">Parking Requirements</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Parking Requirements dictate the minimum number of parking spaces required per dwelling unit and visitor parking regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fddb9a116002f5fba7900393df558bd9</data>
      <data key="d4">Inner_West_LEP_2022.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1756184945</data>
    </node>
    <node id="R1 Zone">
      <data key="d0">R1 Zone</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">R1 Zone is a residential zone subject to specific floor space ratio controls with a maximum FSR of 0.6:1.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fddb9a116002f5fba7900393df558bd9</data>
      <data key="d4">Inner_West_LEP_2022.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1756184945</data>
    </node>
    <node id="R2 Zone">
      <data key="d0">R2 Zone</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">R2 Zone is another residential category defined within the environmental plan, also with a maximum floor space ratio of 0.6:1.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fddb9a116002f5fba7900393df558bd9</data>
      <data key="d4">Inner_West_LEP_2022.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1756184945</data>
    </node>
    <node id="B4 Zone">
      <data key="d0">B4 Zone</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">B4 Zone refers to mixed-use zones with a maximum floor space ratio of 1.2:1 as stipulated in the plan.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fddb9a116002f5fba7900393df558bd9</data>
      <data key="d4">Inner_West_LEP_2022.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1756184945</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Height Controls">
      <data key="d0">Height Controls</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Height Controls refer to specific regulations that limit the maximum allowable heights for residential and commercial buildings within the Inner West Local Environmental Plan 2022.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fddb9a116002f5fba7900393df558bd9</data>
      <data key="d4">Inner_West_LEP_2022.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1756184945</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Setback Requirements">
      <data key="d0">Setback Requirements</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Setback Requirements define the minimum distances that buildings must maintain from property boundaries, including front, side, and rear setbacks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fddb9a116002f5fba7900393df558bd9</data>
      <data key="d4">Inner_West_LEP_2022.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1756184945</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Community Contribution Schemes">
      <data key="d0">Community Contribution Schemes</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Community Contribution Schemes may allow for additional floor space ratio (FSR) in exchange for contributions to community projects, as mentioned in the plan.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fddb9a116002f5fba7900393df558bd9</data>
      <data key="d4">Inner_West_LEP_2022.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1756184946</data>
    </node>
